        "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2\\pi }\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2\\pi }\\operatorname{arcosh}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
